nts to node2 and node3) into a single br0 with STP off and no IP address, making node1 a pure L2 forwarder. Assigned node2's enp8s0 and node3's enp8s0 static addresses 192.168.50.11/24 and 192.168.50.12/24 (persisted via systemd-networkd drop-ins), so the two hosts now share one subnet and reach each other directly with node1 switching frames instead of routing. Completed the mandatory one-node-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes: captured boot-identity baselines, restarted each, confirmed changed boot IDs, and verified post-restart recovery (node1's non-persistent bridge was rebuilt after its own reboot and connectivity re-verified end to end).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected baseline topology: node1 eth1<->node2 enp8s0 and node1 eth2<->node3 enp8s0 were two isolated, unaddressed L2 segments off node1\",\"On node1: stripped docker0's stray 240.127.1.1/24 IP, created br0 with stp_state 0, enslaved eth1 and eth2, brought interfaces up\",\"On node2: added /etc/systemd/network/10-enp8s0.network (static 192.168.50.11/24, DHCP=no) which takes precedence over 50-all-interfaces.network, reloaded networkd\",\"On node3: added /etc/systemd/network/10-enp8s0.network (static 192.168.50.12/24, DHCP=no), reloaded networkd\",\"Verified node2<->node3 ping with TTL=64 (undecremented, proving no L3 hop) and confirmed node1's bridge FDB learned both peer MACs on their respective bridge ports; confirmed br0 carries no IP address\",\"Captured /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id baseline on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node2 via background 'reboot' (ack returned before disconnect), polled until exec available, confirmed boot_id changed, verified static IP persisted and ping to node3 succeeded\",\"Restarted node3 the same way, confirmed boot_id changed, verified static IP persisted and ping to node2 succeeded\",\"Restarted node1 last (SONiC cold reboot, took several minutes), polled until exec available, confirmed boot_id changed\",\"Rebuilt node1's br0 bridge (non-persistent 